      "content": "i don't know if i have the energy for \"rebellion\" anymore. it sounds so exhausting to keep performing just to prove a point to no one. when you look at it from a purely logical perspective, keeping the struggle going just seems like an irrational way to prolong unnecessary suffering. if the play is pointless and the theater is empty, isn't it more logical to just let the curtain fall? it feels like there's no real reason to stick around for an ending that's already been written.",
